              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
            Sources &amp; standards: NEC (NFPA 70) 2023 <strong>Article 705</strong> — load-side interconnection
            <strong>705.12</strong>, with the busbar options in <strong>705.12(B)(3)</strong> and the 120% allowance
            at <strong>705.12(B)(3)(2)</strong>; supply-side connection <strong>705.11</strong>; power control
            systems <strong>705.13</strong>; circuit current and overcurrent protection <strong>690.8</strong> and
            <strong>705.28</strong>. This tool models the <strong>120% option only</strong> — the sum rule, the
            centre-fed allowance, and the engineering-supervision path in 705.12(B)(3) are separate routes with
            their own conditions, and one of them may permit an interconnection this check rejects. The opposite-end
            busbar placement and the permanent warning label are conditions of the allowance, not suggestions. Local
            amendments, the utility's own interconnection agreement, and the AHJ all have final say.
          </p>
